        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): use endsWith instead of includes for _all_ action_id matching",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`isBulkActionsBlock()` uses `el.action_id.includes(\"_all_\")` to detect bulk-action buttons. This has **two bugs**:\n\n1. **False positives**: Action IDs like `\"deploy_all_services\"` or `\"install_all_deps\"` contain the substring `_all_` and are incorrectly treated as bulk actions — their blocks are silently removed from Slack messages.\n2. **False negatives**: Legitimate bulk action IDs like `\"select_all\"` / `\"deselect_all\"` do **not** contain `_all_` (no trailing underscore), so `includes(\"_all_\")` fails to match them.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add shared bulk action-ID grammar in `extensions/slack/src/bulk-action-ids.ts` (`SLACK_BULK_ACTION_ID_SUFFIX`, `isSlackBulkActionId()`).\n- `interactions.block-actions.ts`: classify bulk rows with `isSlackBulkActionId()` (`endsWith(\"_all\")`) instead of substring `includes(\"_all_\")`.\n- Add grammar regression tests plus whole-path Slack confirmation update tests for bulk-row removal and `deploy_all_services` false-positive control.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Current head:** `ffac80ea`\n\n**Unit tests:**\n```\npnpm test extensions/slack/src/bulk-action-ids.test.ts\npnpm test extensions/slack/src/monitor/events/interactions.test.ts -t \"bulk|deploy_all_services\"\n→ 10 passed\n```\n\n**Grammar regression (`isSlackBulkActionId`):**\n\n| action_id | bulk? |\n|-----------|-------|\n| select_all | yes |\n| deselect_all | yes |\n| deploy_all_services | no |\n| install_all_deps | no |\n| approve_selected | no |\n\n**After-fix whole-path message-update proof (handler → `chat.update` blocks):**\n\n1. Last individual selection removes bulk `select_all` / `deselect_all` rows from the updated Slack payload.\n2. A separate `deploy_all_services` row is **not** classified as bulk and remains when another individual control is still present.\n\n**Lint / typecheck:** `npx oxlint` on touched files — clean\n\n## Review\n\n- ClawSweeper review addressed: shared bulk action-ID grammar, whole-path regression, false-positive control\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
